hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1506","We are Bundar, we are Muhammad bin Jafar. H. Amr bin Ali told us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa’id, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’ Al-Muharbibi. He said: We were with Abu Hurairah in the mosque, and a muezzin called the call to prayer, then a man got up and came out and said: “As for this man, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “Peace be upon him.” Bundar said: “He disagreed with Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
